#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "zendesk.integration"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Employee Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in Zendesk caused by changes in OSB.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are added to Zendesk via OSB sync should have appropriate tags.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | liferay.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Liferay                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                            |
	| Group         | Employees                            |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Employees"
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"

Scenario: Remove Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	Removed Liferay employees should have appropriate Zendesk tags.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | liferay.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Liferay                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                            |
	| Group         | Employees                            |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"
	When I update the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to have the role "Agent"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "Agent"
	When I remove the okta user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from the okta group "Employees"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "End User"

Scenario: Deactivate Liferay employee
	Deactivated Liferay employees should have appropriate Zendesk tags.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | liferay.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | Liferay                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                            |
	| Group         | Employees                            |
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_kb" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"
	When I update the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to have the role "Agent"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "Agent"
	When I deactivate the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from okta
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be in the organization "Liferay, Inc."
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not have the "osb_lr_employee" tag
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the name "Liferay Employee1"
	And the user with the email address "liferay.employee1@liferay.com.broken" on zendesk.liferay.com should have the role "End User"